      "problem": "Let $V=C[0,2\\pi ],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,2\\pi ].$ Find $⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the identity $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )).$*",
